          'High-standard kitchens receive daily meat deliveries from authorized, temperature-controlled refrigerated transport vehicles rather than open street markets. In the kitchen, color-coded chopping boards (red for raw meat, yellow for poultry, blue for seafood, green for vegetables, and white for dairy) prevent cross-contamination between raw animal proteins and ready-to-eat items.',
